# ---- Ch III: Approval of DDPs ----
add("DDP/APP/301","III",1,"Who approves a DDP?",
 [["Applicant","Custodian bank wanting to become a DDP"],["Belief","NSDL grants DDP approval"],["Application","Being prepared"],["Question","Who decides?"]],
 "Who grants approval?",
 ["NSDL, as the depository","SEBI","RBI, as banking regulator","The stock exchanges"],1,
 "No person can act as a DDP without SEBI's approval. The application goes through the depository, which forwards it with a recommendation, but SEBI decides.",
 ["The depository forwards and recommends; it doesn't approve.",None,"DDP approval sits with SEBI, not RBI.","Exchanges have no role in DDP approval."],
 "FPI Regs 2019, Reg 10(1)–(3), Reg 13(1)")
add("DDP/APP/302","III",2,"No foreign branches",
 [["Applicant","Indian AD Category-1 bank, registered DP and custodian"],["Overseas presence","No foreign branches"],["Instead","Agency agreements with regulated custodians in 30 countries"],["Question","Does it meet the multinational-presence test?"]],
 "Does it qualify on this test?",
 ["No. It needs its own foreign branches","Yes. Agency relationships with regulated overseas intermediaries count","Only with branches in at least five countries","Only if SEBI waives the test"],1,
 "Reg 11(1)(d) requires a multinational presence either through branches or through agency relationships with overseas intermediaries regulated in their home jurisdictions.",
 ["Branches are one way; regulated agency relationships are the other.",None,"The regulation sets no branch count.","No waiver is needed; the test is met."],
 "FPI Regs 2019, Reg 11(1)(d)")
add("DDP/APP/303","III",2,"SEBI's clock on a DDP application",
 [["SEBI received","Application on 1 June"],["SEBI asked for","Further information on 15 June"],["Received","8 July"],["Question","Latest decision date"]],
 "By when should SEBI decide?",
 ["1 July","Within 30 days of 8 July","Within 7 working days of 8 July","There's no time limit"],1,
 "SEBI disposes of a DDP application as soon as possible and no later than 30 days after receipt, or after the further information is furnished, whichever is later.",
 ["The clock runs from the later date, when the information arrived.",None,"7 working days isn't the decision window.","Reg 13(2) sets a 30-day limit."],
 "FPI Regs 2019, Reg 12, Reg 13(2)")
add("DDP/SUR/304","III",2,"DDP wants to give up its approval",
 [["DDP","Exiting the custody business"],["FPI clients","120"],["Request","Surrender DDP approval"],["Question","What can SEBI do?"]],
 "What happens on surrender?",
 ["Surrender takes effect on notice","SEBI may accept it with conditions to protect clients and the market","Surrender isn't allowed while clients remain","Only RBI can accept it"],1,
 "A DDP may ask SEBI to accept surrender of its approval. While accepting, SEBI may impose conditions it considers fit to protect investors, the DDP's clients or the securities market, and the DDP must comply.",
 ["Surrender needs SEBI's acceptance.",None,"Surrender is allowed, subject to SEBI's conditions.","SEBI, not RBI, handles DDP approvals."],
 "FPI Regs 2019, Reg 18")
add("DDP/APP/305","III",2,"Incomplete DDP application",
 [["Applicant","Proposed DDP"],["Gap","Missing details of its AML systems"],["SEBI's view","Application is deficient"],["Question","Can SEBI reject straight away?"]],
 "What must SEBI do before rejecting?",
 ["Nothing; deficient applications are rejected outright","Give the applicant a reasonable opportunity to remove the deficiency within a set time","Refer it back to the depository for a new recommendation","Approve it provisionally"],1,
 "A deficient DDP application is liable to be rejected, but before rejecting, SEBI gives the applicant a reasonable opportunity to remove the deficiency within the time it specifies.",
 ["Reg 14 requires a chance to fix the deficiency first.",None,"The regulation doesn't require a fresh depository recommendation.","There's no provisional approval."],
 "FPI Regs 2019, Reg 14")
add("DDP/APP/306","III",1,"No anti-money-laundering systems",
 [["Applicant","Custodian bank, DP, AD Category-1"],["Gap","No systems to comply with FATF standards and PMLA"],["Plan","Build them after approval"],["Question","Eligible now?"]],
 "Is it eligible?",
 ["Yes; systems can follow approval","No. AML systems are an eligibility condition","Yes, if it hires a compliance officer","Only for Category II clients"],1,
 "Reg 11(1)(e) requires a DDP applicant to have systems and procedures to comply with FATF standards, PMLA and SEBI circulars before approval.",
 ["The systems are a precondition, not a follow-up.",None,"A compliance officer alone doesn't meet the systems test.","Eligibility applies to the DDP as a whole."],
 "FPI Regs 2019, Reg 11(1)(e)")

# ---- Ch IV: Investment conditions ----
add("INV/ELG/401","IV",1,"Which of these can't an FPI buy?",
 [["FPI","Category I fund"],["Shortlist","REIT units, Indian Depository Receipts, exchange-traded index futures, private unlisted company shares"],["Route","FPI account"],["Question","Which one is outside the FPI route?"]],
 "Which is not permitted through the FPI route?",
 ["REIT units","Indian Depository Receipts","Exchange-traded index futures","Shares of a private unlisted company"],3,
 "Reg 20(1) lets FPIs invest in listed or to-be-listed shares, mutual fund units, CIS units, exchange-traded derivatives, REIT, InvIT and Category III AIF units, IDRs, and permitted debt. Private unlisted shares aren't on the list; buying them is FDI.",
 ["REIT units are permitted under Reg 20(1)(e).","Indian Depository Receipts are permitted under Reg 20(1)(f).","Exchange-traded derivatives are permitted under Reg 20(1)(d).",None],
 "FPI Regs 2019, Reg 20(1)")
add("INV/IPO/402","IV",3,"Pre-listing shares after an IPO",
 [["FPI","Held unlisted shares since before the 2019 Regulations"],["Event","The company lists through an IPO"],["FDI investors","Face a lock-in on similar shares"],["Question","Does a lock-in apply to the FPI?"]],
 "What applies?",
 ["No lock-in; FPIs are exempt","The same lock-in as an FDI investor in a similar position","A fixed one-year lock-in","A lock-in only if the stake is over 10%"],1,
 "Where an FPI held unlisted equity before the Regulations began and continues to hold it after the IPO and listing, those shares are locked in for the same period that applies to an FDI investor in a similar position.",
 ["Reg 20(2) applies the FDI lock-in.",None,"The period mirrors the FDI rule; it isn't a fixed year.","The lock-in doesn't depend on stake size."],
 "FPI Regs 2019, Reg 20(2)")
add("INV/DMT/403","IV",2,"Rights entitlements not in demat",
 [["FPI","Category II fund"],["Holding","Rights entitlements, not dematerialised"],["Rule of thumb","FPIs hold securities only in demat form"],["Question","Is this allowed?"]],
 "Can the FPI hold them this way?",
 ["No. Everything must be in demat","Yes. Rights entitlements may be held or transferred in non-demat form","Only for 30 days","Only with SEBI approval"],1,
 "FPIs hold securities only in demat form, but a proviso allows all rights entitlements to be held or transferred in non-dematerialised form. Old physical shares that can't be dematerialised may also stay physical.",
 ["The proviso specifically exempts rights entitlements.",None,"There's no 30-day limit.","No SEBI approval is needed."],
 "FPI Regs 2019, Reg 20(4)(e) and provisos")
add("INV/SET/404","IV",2,"Selling before settlement",
 [["FPI","Category I fund"],["Monday","Buys 50,000 shares"],["Monday afternoon","Price spikes; wants to sell the same shares"],["Settlement","Not yet complete"]],
 "Can it sell now?",
 ["Yes, through a registered broker","No. FPIs can't sell against open purchases; they sell after settlement","Yes, up to half the quantity","Yes, if it borrows the shares under SLB"],1,
 "FPIs can't short sell except under SLB or another SEBI framework, and sales against open purchases aren't permitted. FPIs can sell such securities only after settlement.",
 ["A broker doesn't change the open-purchase rule.",None,"There's no partial allowance.","Borrowing creates a different position. It doesn't let it sell the unsettled purchase itself."],
 "Op. Guidelines Part C 5")
add("INV/OFF/405","IV",2,"Moving shares between sister registrations",
 [["Owner","Pension fund with three FPI registrations under a multiple-manager structure"],["PAN","Same for all three"],["Request","Move shares off-market from one registration to another"],["Through","Its DDP"]],
 "Can the DDP process it?",
 ["No. All FPI transfers must be on exchange","Yes. Off-market transfers between such FPIs with the same PAN are allowed","Only with SEBI's approval","Only for debt securities"],1,
 "FPIs under a multiple-manager structure with the same PAN may request off-market transfers between themselves through their DDPs. Approval is without prejudice to tax.",
 ["Off-market transfers are allowed in this case.",None,"The DDP processes them; SEBI approval isn't needed.","It isn't limited to debt."],
 "Op. Guidelines Part C 3(i)–(ii); FPI Regs 2019, Reg 20(4)(d)(xiii)")
add("INV/SHT/406","IV",1,"Plain short selling",
 [["FPI","Category II hedge fund"],["Plan","Sell shares it doesn't own, without borrowing"],["Segment","Cash market"],["Question","Allowed?"]],
 "Is naked short selling allowed?",
 ["Yes, for hedge funds","No. Short selling is only allowed under SLB or another SEBI framework","Yes, if covered by month-end","Yes, up to 5% of holdings"],1,
 "FPIs aren't allowed to short sell in the Indian market except as permitted under securities lending and borrowing or another SEBI framework.",
 ["Hedge funds get no exception.",None,"Covering later doesn't make it permitted.","There's no percentage allowance."],
 "Op. Guidelines Part C 5; FPI Regs 2019, Reg 20(4)(b)(ii)")
add("INV/IPO/407","IV",3,"IPO bids from sister registrations",
 [["Bidder","Pension fund with two registrations under a multiple-manager structure"],["Bids","Two IPO bids, same PAN, different demat accounts"],["Registrar's concern","Multiple bids"],["Question","Are they treated as multiple bids?"]],
 "How are the bids treated?",
 ["As multiple bids; one is rejected","Not as multiple bids, but the 10% check runs on the PAN","Only the larger bid counts","Both are rejected"],1,
 "Bids by FPIs under a multiple-manager structure with the same PAN but different demat accounts may not be treated as multiple bids. At allotment, registrars check the single-FPI limit using PAN and validate investor-group limits with the depositories.",
 ["The guidelines say such bids may not be treated as multiple bids.",None,"Both can count, subject to the limit check.","There's no basis to reject both."],
 "Op. Guidelines Part C 6(ii)–(iii)")
add("INV/RE/408","IV",2,"Selling rights entitlements",
 [["FPI","Category I fund"],["Holding","Rights entitlements in a listed company"],["Plan","Transfer them to a related party at a nominal price"],["Question","What price rule applies?"]],
 "At what price must it transfer them?",
 ["Any agreed price","Market price or fair value, as applicable","Face value","Zero, if related"],1,
 "An FPI must make sure rights entitlements are transferred at market price or fair value, as applicable. Transfers of rights entitlements are also exempt from the broker requirement.",
 ["The price can't be anything agreed.",None,"Face value isn't the rule.","Relatedness doesn't permit a nominal price."],
 "Op. Guidelines Part C 7; FPI Regs 2019, Reg 20(4)(d)(xi)")
add("INV/MRG/409","IV",3,"Margin timing for a family office",
 [["FPI","Category II family office"],["Trade","Cash-market purchase"],["Assumption","FPI trades are margined on T+1"],["Question","Correct for this FPI?"]],
 "How is it margined?",
 ["T+1, like all FPIs","Upfront, like non-institutional trades","T+2","No margin for FPIs"],1,
 "FPI trades are generally margined on a T+1 basis, but trades of Category II FPIs that are corporate bodies, individuals or family offices are margined upfront, like non-institutional trades.",
 ["T+1 applies to most FPIs, not this sub-category.",None,"T+2 isn't the rule.","FPI trades are margined."],
 "Op. Guidelines Part C 8(i)")
add("INV/DBT/410","IV",2,"Bond that never lists",
 [["FPI","Category I fund"],["Bought","To-be-listed corporate bonds without end-use checks"],["Day 35","Bonds still not listed"],["Question","What now?"]],
 "What must the FPI do?",
 ["Nothing; listing can come later","Dispose of the bonds immediately to a domestic investor or the issuer","Convert them to FDI","Hold them but stop coupon receipts"],1,
 "FPIs can buy to-be-listed corporate debt without the end-use restrictions for unlisted debt. If listing doesn't happen within 30 days, or the issue fails the end-use restriction, the FPI must immediately dispose of it to a domestic investor or the issuer.",
 ["The 30-day window has passed.",None,"Debt doesn't convert to FDI.","There's no rule about stopping coupons."],
 "Op. Guidelines Part C 9(iii)")
add("INV/DBT/411","IV",3,"Debt mutual fund units",
 [["FPI","Category II fund"],["Investment","Units of an Indian debt-oriented mutual fund"],["Assumption","Mutual fund units don't use corporate debt limits"],["Question","Correct?"]],
 "How are these units counted?",
 ["As equity","As investment in corporate debt","Outside all limits","As government securities"],1,
 "FPI investments in debt-oriented mutual fund schemes are reckoned as investments in corporate debt.",
 ["They count as corporate debt, not equity.",None,"They're inside the corporate debt limits.","They aren't treated as G-Secs."],
 "Op. Guidelines Part C 9(iv)")
add("INV/AGG/412","IV",3,"Sectoral cap breached",
 [["Company","Listed company in a capped sector"],["Event","FPI purchases push total foreign holding past the sectoral cap"],["FPIs identified","Net buyers on the breach day"],["Question","How do they fix it?"]],
 "What's the fix?",
 ["Sell to any buyer within 30 days","Sell the excess within 5 trading days, only to domestic investors, shared proportionately among net buyers","The exchange cancels the last trades","The company issues new shares to dilute"],1,
 "In a breach of the sectoral cap or aggregate FPI or NRI limit, foreign investors divest the excess within 5 trading days of settlement, selling only to domestic investors. The excess is spread proportionately across the foreign investors that were net buyers on the breach day.",
 ["The window is 5 trading days, and sales go to domestic investors.",None,"Exchange trades in breach aren't annulled.","Dilution isn't the prescribed fix."],
 "Op. Guidelines Part C 2(N)–(O), (X)")
add("INV/AGG/413","IV",3,"Headroom comes back mid-window",
 [["FPI","Told to sell 20,000 excess shares after a cap breach"],["Day 3","Other FPIs sell; holdings are back within the cap"],["FPI asks","Can we keep our shares now?"],["Window","5 trading days"]],
 "Does the obligation fall away?",
 ["Yes, since there's no breach any more","No. It must still divest within the window","Yes, if it applies to SEBI","Only half must be sold"],1,
 "If foreign shareholding comes back within limits during the divestment period because others sold, the FPIs advised to divest must still do so within the period, even though headroom has reappeared.",
 ["The guidelines say the obligation stands despite new headroom.",None,"There's no application route.","The full advised quantity must be sold."],
 "Op. Guidelines Part C 2(W)")
add("INV/AGG/414","IV",2,"Red flag on a stock",
 [["Company","Listed mid-cap"],["Status","Foreign holding within 3% of its aggregate FPI limit"],["Exchange","Shows remaining headroom in shares"],["Question","What does this mean for FPIs?"]],
 "What does the red flag mean?",
 ["FPIs can't buy at all","FPIs may buy, knowing a breach means selling the excess within 5 trading days","Trades will be reversed if the limit is crossed","Only Category I FPIs may buy"],1,
 "A red flag is activated when headroom is 3% or less of the aggregate FPI or NRI limit or sectoral cap. Foreign investors may still trade, but consciously: if a breach follows, they must divest the excess within 5 trading days of settlement. Purchases halt only once a limit is actually breached.",
 ["Buying stops only after a breach, not at the red flag.",None,"Trades aren't annulled.","Both categories may trade."],
 "Op. Guidelines Part C 2(K)–(M)")
add("INV/FDI/415","IV",3,"Group chooses FDI treatment",
 [["FPI group","Now holds 11% of a listed company"],["Choice","Treat the whole holding as FDI instead of selling down"],["Plan","Later sell part of it on the exchange through the FPI account"],["Question","What applies after the choice?"]],
 "What changes after choosing FDI?",
 ["Nothing; it can keep trading as an FPI","No further portfolio investment in that company; sales only through the route it was acquired, with LEC reporting","It must sell everything within 180 days","It needs RBI approval for every trade"],1,
 "If an FPI and its group reach 10% or more and opt to treat their investment as FDI, they make no further portfolio investment in that company. The custodian reports the choice; holdings are marked FDI, can be sold only through the route they were acquired, and the custodian makes LEC reporting.",
 ["Electing FDI ends portfolio investment in that company.",None,"There's no forced exit.","Trade-by-trade RBI approval isn't required."],
 "Op. Guidelines Part C 16; FPI Regs 2019, Reg 20(7), Reg 22(3)")
add("INV/GRP/416","IV",2,"Individual FPI and a sister",
 [["FPI A","Individual investor, 6% of Company Z"],["FPI B","Her sister, also registered as an FPI, 5% of Company Z"],["Common ownership","None (separate individuals)"],["Question","Are they clubbed?"]],
 "Are they one investor group?",
 ["No. Separate individuals are never clubbed","Yes. An individual FPI and relatives registered as FPIs count as one investor group","Only if they share a demat account","Only if one funds the other"],1,
 "For individuals registered as FPIs, the individual and relatives who are also registered as FPIs are considered together as an investor group. 'Relative' follows Section 2(77) of the Companies Act, 2013. Together they're at 11%.",
 ["Relatives are clubbed for individual FPIs.",None,"Clubbing doesn't depend on a shared account.","Funding isn't the test; the relationship is."],
 "Op. Guidelines Part C 1(i)")
add("INV/GRP/417","IV",2,"World Bank entities and clubbing",
 [["FPIs","IFC and IBRD, both registered"],["Holdings","IFC 6% and IBRD 5% of the same company"],["Common control","Both World Bank Group"],["Question","Breach of 10%?"]],
 "Is this a breach?",
 ["Yes. World Bank Group entities are one investor group","No. World Bank Group entities are exempt from clubbing for the 10% limit","Yes, unless RBI approves","Only if they share a custodian"],1,
 "A Government of India letter exempts World Bank Group entities (IBRD, IDA, MIGA and IFC) from clubbing of investment limits for the below-10% FPI limit in a single company.",
 ["They're specifically exempt from clubbing.",None,"The exemption comes from the Government; no RBI approval is needed.","Custodians don't affect the exemption."],
 "Op. Guidelines Part C 1(viii)")
add("INV/GRP/418","IV",3,"Two provincial government funds",
 [["FPI A","Fund of a Canadian province"],["FPI B","Fund of another province in the same country"],["Beneficial owners","Different, identified under PMLA rules"],["Question","Clubbed as government-related?"]],
 "Are they clubbed?",
 ["Yes. Same country, same government group","No. Provincial entities with different beneficial owners aren't clubbed","Yes, unless each is under 5%","Only if they share a manager"],1,
 "Investments by foreign governments or their related entities from provinces or states of federal countries aren't clubbed if they have different beneficial owners identified under PMLA rules.",
 ["Different BOs keep them separate.",None,"There's no 5% threshold here.","A shared manager isn't the test."],
 "Op. Guidelines Part C 1(ix)")
add("INV/GRP/419","IV",2,"Group spread across two custodians",
 [["FPI A","Custodied at Bank X"],["FPI B","Same group, custodied at Bank Y"],["Concern","Neither custodian sees the full group position"],["Question","How is the 10% limit monitored?"]],
 "How is it monitored?",
 ["Each custodian checks only its own client","Custodians report to both depositories, which club holdings and monitor them daily","The FPIs self-report monthly","SEBI checks at continuance"],1,
 "Where group FPIs use different custodians, the custodians report holdings to both depositories. The depositories club the group's investments, monitor them on an end-of-day basis, and report breaches to SEBI. Group FPIs can ask NSDL for the group's aggregate holding before investing.",
 ["Depositories combine the data, not individual custodians.",None,"Monitoring is daily by the depositories.","It's daily, not at continuance."],
 "Op. Guidelines Part C 1(ii)–(vii); FPI Regs 2019, Reg 25(2)(d)")
add("INV/ODI/420","IV",3,"FPI and ODI positions in one company",
 [["Investor","Holds 7% of Company Q as an FPI"],["Also","ODI positions referencing 4% of Company Q"],["View","ODI exposure is separate, so no breach"],["Question","Correct?"]],
 "How is the 10% limit applied?",
 ["Separately to FPI holdings and ODI positions","To FPI holdings and ODI positions together","To FPI holdings only","To ODI positions only"],1,
 "The below-10% limit applies to ODI subscribers too, and where an investor has both FPI investments and ODI positions in the same company, the limit applies to the two together. At 11%, this investor is over.",
 ["The guidelines club FPI and ODI exposure.",None,"ODI positions count too.","FPI holdings count too."],
 "Op. Guidelines Part D 1(viii)")
add("INV/ODI/421","IV",3,"Custom basket hedged in India",
 [["ODI issuer","Category I FPI"],["Product","Swap on a custom basket, 8% Indian stocks"],["Hedge","Indian component hedged onshore"],["Question","Is it an ODI?"]],
 "Is this an ODI?",
 ["No. Indian weight is under 20%","Yes. Custom baskets hedged onshore are always ODIs","No, unless Indian weight exceeds 50%","Only if sold to Indian residents"],1,
 "For non-proprietary indices like MSCI World, trades with less than 20% Indian weight aren't treated as ODIs. Custom baskets hedged onshore are always ODIs, whatever the Indian share. ODI rules have been revised since the 2019 guidelines, so confirm against the current Master Circular.",
 ["The 20% threshold is for non-proprietary indices, not custom baskets.",None,"There's no 50% test.","ODI status doesn't depend on buyer residence."],
 "Op. Guidelines Part D 1(v)","Y")

# ---- Ch V: FPI obligations ----
add("OBL/RPT/501","V",1,"False information discovered",
 [["FPI","Category II fund"],["Discovery","An ownership figure in its application was wrong"],["Found","On 2 May"],["Question","Deadline to inform SEBI and the DDP"]],
 "What's the deadline?",
 ["At continuance","As soon as possible, within 7 working days","Within 30 days","Only if the DDP asks"],1,
 "An FPI must inform SEBI and its DDP in writing, as soon as possible and within 7 working days, if information it submitted earlier is found to be false or misleading in any material respect.",
 ["Waiting for continuance breaches the deadline.",None,"The deadline is 7 working days.","The duty doesn't depend on being asked."],
 "FPI Regs 2019, Reg 22(1)(b)")
add("OBL/KYC/502","V",2,"KYC on the fund's own investors",
 [["FPI","Luxembourg fund"],["Its investors","2,000 unit holders"],["Question","Whose rules govern KYC on them?"],["DDP","Asks for confirmation"]],
 "Which rules apply to KYC on its own investors?",
 ["Indian KYC rules","The rules of the jurisdiction where the FPI is organised","No KYC is needed on its investors","The DDP's internal policy"],1,
 "An FPI must undertake necessary KYC on its shareholders or investors under the rules of the jurisdiction where it is organised. It must also give BO details when SEBI, the DDP or enforcement agencies ask.",
 ["Home-jurisdiction rules govern its own investor KYC.",None,"KYC on its investors is required.","The DDP's policy governs the DDP's own KYC, not this."],
 "FPI Regs 2019, Reg 22(1)(i)–(j)")
add("OBL/COC/503","V",2,"Mixing client and house money",
 [["FPI","Regulated asset manager, Category I"],["Practice","Holds its own and clients' securities in one pool"],["Reason","Operational simplicity"],["Question","Allowed under the code of conduct?"]],
 "Is it allowed?",
 ["Yes, if records are kept","No. The code requires clear segregation of own and client money and securities","Yes, for Category I FPIs","Only if clients consent"],1,
 "The FPI code of conduct requires clear segregation of the FPI's own money and securities from its clients', and an arm's-length relationship between its fund-management business and other businesses.",
 ["Record-keeping doesn't replace segregation.",None,"The code applies to all FPIs.","Client consent doesn't override the code."],
 "FPI Regs 2019, Third Schedule, para 4")
add("OBL/COC/504","V",1,"Director's family trades on a tip",
 [["FPI","Category II fund"],["Event","A director's relative trades on unpublished price-sensitive information"],["Director","Says the relative isn't the FPI"],["Question","Code of conduct issue?"]],
 "Is this a breach?",
 ["No. The relative isn't the FPI","Yes. The code bars insider trading through associates, family, relatives or friends","Only if the FPI profited","Only if SEBI files charges"],1,
 "The code bars the FPI and its directors or managers from insider trading through their own accounts or through associates, family members, relatives or friends. It also bars passing price-sensitive information.",
 ["Trading through relatives is expressly covered.",None,"Profit isn't required for a breach.","The obligation exists regardless of charges."],
 "FPI Regs 2019, Third Schedule, paras 9–10")
add("OBL/CO/505","V",2,"Compliance officer spots a breach",
 [["Officer","FPI's compliance officer"],["Finding","The fund bought securities outside its permitted list"],["Management","Asks to wait until the quarterly board meeting"],["Question","What must the officer do?"]],
 "What's the officer's duty?",
 ["Wait for the board meeting","Report it immediately and independently to SEBI and the DDP","Report only to the global custodian","Fix it quietly and log it"],1,
 "The compliance officer must immediately and independently report any non-compliance observed to SEBI and the DDP.",
 ["The duty is immediate, not quarterly.",None,"The report goes to SEBI and the DDP.","Fixing it doesn't replace reporting."],
 "FPI Regs 2019, Reg 27(2)")
add("OBL/REC/506","V",2,"Records an FPI must keep",
 [["FPI","Category I fund"],["Records kept","Remittance accounts, bank statements, contract notes, intermediary emails"],["Auditor suggests","Also needed?"],["Question","Which isn't a required record?"]],
 "Which is not on the required list?",
 ["Accounts of remittances and gains or losses","Bank statements","Contract notes","Board minutes of every investee company"],3,
 "Reg 29 lists the FPI's required records: accounts of remittances and realised gains or losses, bank statements, contract notes, and communications with DDPs, brokers and DPs. Investee companies' board minutes aren't on it.",
 ["Remittance accounts are required under Reg 29(a).","Bank statements are required under Reg 29(b).","Contract notes are required under Reg 29(c).",None],
 "FPI Regs 2019, Reg 29")
add("OBL/GRP/507","V",2,"New sister fund joins the group",
 [["FPI","Category II fund"],["Event","Its parent launches another FPI it owns 70% of"],["Effect","The two are now an investor group"],["Question","When must the DDP know?"]],
 "What's the deadline?",
 ["At next continuance","As soon as possible, within 7 working days","Only when combined holdings near 10%","Within 90 days"],1,
 "Any direct or indirect change in common ownership or control of the FPI or its investor group must be brought to the DDP's notice as soon as possible and within 7 working days. The FPI must keep accurate investor-group details with the DDP at all times.",
 ["Continuance is too late.",None,"The duty doesn't wait for the 10% limit.","The deadline is 7 working days."],
 "FPI Regs 2019, Reg 22(1)(c), (l), Reg 22(5)")
add("OBL/SEG/508","V",3,"New sub-fund starts investing",
 [["FPI","Umbrella fund with ring-fenced sub-funds"],["Event","Launches a new sub-fund that will invest in India"],["Plan","Send BO details at next continuance"],["Question","When are BO details due?"]],
 "When must BO details be given?",
 ["At next continuance","Before the new sub-fund invests in India","Within 30 days of its first trade","Never; the umbrella's details suffice"],1,
 "FPIs with segregated portfolios give a BO declaration for each sub-fund or share class that invests in India. For a new one, BO information must be given before investing in India through it.",
 ["Continuance is too late for a new sub-fund.",None,"It's due before the first investment, not after.","Each investing sub-fund needs its own declaration."],
 "Op. Guidelines Part A 13(i)")
add("OBL/SEG/509","V",1,"Sub-fund wound up",
 [["FPI","Umbrella fund"],["Event","Closes a sub-fund that invested in India"],["Question","Who needs to know, and when?"],["Holdings","Already sold"]],
 "What's required?",
 ["Nothing","Intimate the DDP forthwith","Tell SEBI at continuance","Apply for fresh registration"],1,
 "When a sub-fund, share class or equivalent structure that invests in India is deleted, the FPI must intimate the DDP forthwith.",
 ["Deletion must be reported.",None,"The DDP must be told forthwith, not at continuance.","No fresh registration is needed."],
 "Op. Guidelines Part A 13(iii)")
add("OBL/DIS/510","V",2,"Dispute with the DDP",
 [["FPI","Category I fund"],["Dispute","Fees and a delayed corporate action"],["FPI plan","Sue the DDP in a foreign court"],["Question","What route do the regulations set?"]],
 "Which route applies?",
 ["Any court the FPI chooses","SEBI's dispute resolution mechanism: mediation, conciliation and/or arbitration","RBI's banking ombudsman","The stock exchange's investor panel"],1,
 "Claims or disputes between an FPI and a DDP about the DDP's securities-market activities go to a dispute resolution mechanism with mediation, conciliation and/or arbitration, under SEBI's procedure.",
 ["Reg 24A sets SEBI's mechanism.",None,"The banking ombudsman isn't the specified route.","Exchange panels aren't the specified route."],
 "FPI Regs 2019, Reg 24A")
add("OBL/CUS/511","V",2,"Who signs the custody agreement?",
 [["FPI","Category II fund"],["Arrangement","Its global custodian handles all relationships"],["Question","Can the global custodian sign the local custody agreement?"],["Timing","Before first investment"]],
 "Who may sign?",
 ["Only the FPI itself","The FPI, or a global custodian acting on its behalf, before any investment","Only the DDP","Nobody; no agreement is needed"],1,
 "An FPI, or a global custodian acting on its behalf, must enter into an agreement with the DDP to act as custodian before making any investment.",
 ["A global custodian acting for it may sign.",None,"The DDP is the counterparty, not the signer for the FPI.","An agreement is required before investing."],
 "FPI Regs 2019, Reg 25(1)")

# ---- Ch VI: DDP obligations ----
add("DDO/BLK/601","VI",1,"Lapsed registration places an order",
 [["Client","FPI whose registration lapsed last month"],["Order","Buy 10,000 shares"],["Custodian","Its DDP"],["Question","What must the DDP do?"]],
 "What's the DDP's duty?",
 ["Process it; renewal can follow","Block it; only registered FPIs may invest","Process it if the FPI promises to renew","Ask SEBI first"],1,
 "A DDP must ensure that only registered FPIs are allowed to invest in the securities market.",
 ["The DDP can't let an unregistered entity invest.",None,"A promise doesn't restore registration.","The duty is the DDP's own; it doesn't need SEBI first."],
 "FPI Regs 2019, Reg 31(1)(e)")
add("DDO/COI/602","VI",2,"Registration team and sales team",
 [["DDP","Custodian bank"],["Proposal","Relationship managers approve FPI registrations to speed up onboarding"],["Concern","Conflict of interest"],["Question","Allowed?"]],
 "Is it allowed?",
 ["Yes, if the RM is senior","No. The DDP must segregate registration from its other activities to avoid conflicts","Yes, for Category I only","Yes, with client consent"],1,
 "A DDP must segregate activities so there's no conflict of interest between granting FPI registration as a DDP and its other activities.",
 ["Seniority doesn't remove the conflict.",None,"The rule applies to all registrations.","Client consent doesn't override the segregation duty."],
 "FPI Regs 2019, Reg 31(3)")
add("DDO/RPT/603","VI",2,"Monthly applications report",
 [["DDP","Received 40 FPI applications in March"],["Report","Monthly report on applications to SEBI"],["Question","When is March's report due?"],["Format","Prescribed annexure"]],
 "When is it due?",
 ["31 March","By 10 April","By 30 April","With the annual audit"],1,
 "Every DDP sends SEBI a monthly report on applications received from FPI applicants. The report for a month is due by the 10th of the following month.",
 ["It covers the full month, so it can't be due on its last day.",None,"The deadline is the 10th.","It's monthly, not annual."],
 "Op. Guidelines Part A 9(i); FPI Regs 2019, Reg 31(4)")
add("DDO/RPT/604","VI",2,"Daily transaction reporting",
 [["Custodian","Services 300 FPIs"],["Question","How often must it report FPI transactions?"],["To whom","Depositories and SEBI"],["Current practice","Weekly batches"]],
 "What's required?",
 ["Weekly is fine","Daily","Monthly","Only on request"],1,
 "The custodian reports to the depositories and SEBI, on a daily basis, the transactions entered into by FPIs. It also monitors FPI investments and keeps true and fair records.",
 ["Weekly batches don't meet the daily requirement.",None,"Monthly is too infrequent.","Reporting is routine, not on request."],
 "FPI Regs 2019, Reg 25(2)(a)–(c)")
add("DDO/AUD/605","VI",2,"What the annual review covers",
 [["DDP","Approved custodian bank"],["Review","Annual review by an independent professional"],["Draft scope","IT security only"],["Question","Is the scope enough?"]],
 "What must the review cover?",
 ["IT security only","Systems and procedures for meeting obligations to clients, regulators and others, and compliance with the regulations","Financial statements only","Only complaints received"],1,
 "The annual independent review covers the DDP's systems, procedures and controls for meeting its obligations to clients, regulators and other bodies, and its compliance with the regulations and circulars.",
 ["The scope is wider than IT security.",None,"It's a systems and compliance review, not a financial audit.","Complaints are only part of it."],
 "FPI Regs 2019, Reg 31(5) and Explanation")
add("DDO/REC/606","VI",2,"Where the DDP keeps its records",
 [["DDP","Moving FPI registration records to a new data centre"],["Question","Does SEBI need to know?"],["Retention","Records kept indefinitely"],["Format","Physical and electronic"]],
 "What's required?",
 ["Nothing","Intimate SEBI in writing of the location where records are kept","Get RBI's approval","Tell each FPI"],1,
 "A DDP must intimate SEBI in writing of the location where books, records and documents are kept, and preserve them at all times.",
 ["SEBI must be told the location.",None,"RBI approval isn't the requirement.","The duty is to SEBI, not clients."],
 "FPI Regs 2019, Reg 32(2)–(3)")
add("DDO/MAN/607","VI",1,"Does a DDP need a manual?",
 [["DDP","Newly approved"],["Procedures","Held informally by the team"],["Question","Is a written manual required?"],["Inspection","Due next year"]],
 "Is a manual required?",
 ["No. Informal procedures are fine","Yes. A manual of its systems and procedures is required","Only after the first inspection","Only for DDPs with over 100 clients"],1,
 "Every DDP must have a manual setting out the systems and procedures for discharging its functions, along with adequate infrastructure, staff and systems, and mechanisms to review its controls.",
 ["The guidelines require a written manual.",None,"It's needed from the start.","There's no client-count threshold."],
 "Op. Guidelines Part A 8(ii)")
add("DDO/REJ/608","VI",2,"Recording a rejection",
 [["DDP","Rejects an FPI application for sanctions concerns"],["Question","Where does the rejection reason go?"],["Other DDPs","May receive the same applicant"],["Database","Kept by NSDL and CDSL"]],
 "What must the DDP do?",
 ["Keep the reason internal","Record the reason in the depositories' applicant database, visible to all DDPs","Email other DDPs directly","Publish it on its website"],1,
 "The depositories keep a database of FPI applicants. Every DDP inputs applicant details and, where it rejects an application, records the reason, which all DDPs can see.",
 ["The reason must go in the shared database.",None,"The database is the channel, not email.","Public disclosure isn't the requirement."],
 "Op. Guidelines Part A 7(ii)")
add("DDO/CO/609","VI",1,"DDP's compliance officer finds a breach",
 [["DDP","Custodian bank"],["Finding","FPI accounts opened before KYC was complete"],["Officer","DDP's compliance officer"],["Question","Who must be told?"]],
 "What must the officer do?",
 ["Report only to the DDP's board","Report immediately and independently to SEBI","Report to each FPI affected","Wait for the annual review"],1,
 "Every DDP appoints a compliance officer who must immediately and independently report any non-compliance observed to SEBI.",
 ["Reporting internally isn't enough.",None,"The duty runs to SEBI.","It's immediate."],
 "FPI Regs 2019, Reg 33")
add("DDO/SIG/610","VI",1,"Naming the signatory",
 [["DDP","Approving an FPI registration"],["Approval letter","Doesn't name who signed"],["FPI asks","Who approved this?"],["Question","Is the letter complete?"]],
 "What's missing?",
 ["Nothing","The name of the DDP's signatory or signatories","SEBI's countersignature","The FPI's PAN"],1,
 "The DDP must mention the name of its signatory or signatories in the FPI registration approval it communicates to the FPI.",
 ["The guidelines require the signatory's name.",None,"SEBI doesn't countersign DDP approvals.","PAN isn't the missing requirement here."],
 "Op. Guidelines Part A 2(vii)")
add("DDO/INS/611","VI",2,"SEBI inspection without notice",
 [["DDP","Custodian bank"],["Notice","Usually at least 10 days"],["Situation","SEBI orders an inspection with no notice"],["Question","Is that allowed?"]],
 "Can SEBI inspect without notice?",
 ["No. 10 days' notice is always required","Yes, by written order, if satisfied it's in investors' interest","Only with RBI's consent","Only during market hours"],1,
 "SEBI normally gives at least 10 days' notice before inspecting a DDP, but it can direct an inspection without notice, by written order, where satisfied that's in investors' interest.",
 ["The proviso allows no-notice inspections.",None,"RBI's consent isn't required.","There's no market-hours condition."],
 "FPI Regs 2019, Reg 37(1)")
add("DDO/INS/612","VI",3,"Who pays for the inspection?",
 [["SEBI","Appoints an outside auditor to inspect a DDP"],["Cost","Auditor's fees plus expenses"],["DDP's view","SEBI should bear it"],["Question","Who pays?"]],
 "Who bears the cost?",
 ["SEBI","The DDP; SEBI may recover the expenses, including auditor fees","The depository","The FPI clients"],1,
 "SEBI may recover from the DDP the expenses it incurs in inspecting or investigating its books, records and systems, including fees paid to auditors.",
 ["SEBI can recover the cost.",None,"The depository doesn't pay.","Clients aren't charged."],
 "FPI Regs 2019, Reg 41–42")
add("DDO/MED/613","VI",1,"DDP employee on a podcast",
 [["Speaker","Head of custody at a DDP"],["Statement","Recommends a listed bank stock"],["Employer","Holds that stock"],["Disclosure","None"]],
 "What was required?",
 ["Nothing; DDPs don't manage money","Disclosure of interests, including the employer's and family's positions","SEBI's pre-approval of the podcast","A disclaimer only"],1,
 "A DDP or its employees can't give investment advice in public media without disclosing their interest, including long or short positions. An employee also discloses the interests of dependent family and the employer.",
 ["The disclosure rule applies to DDPs too.",None,"No pre-approval is needed, only disclosure.","A generic disclaimer doesn't disclose the actual interest."],
 "FPI Regs 2019, Reg 35")

# ---- Fees ----
add("FEE/ADV/701","FEE",2,"How continuance fees are collected",
 [["DDP","Services 200 FPIs"],["Question","How often does it collect registration fees from them?"],["Practice proposed","Yearly instalments"],["Remittance","To SEBI"]],
 "What's the rule?",
 ["Yearly instalments","In advance, once every three years","Once, at first registration","Monthly"],1,
 "DDPs collect registration fees from FPIs in advance once every three years and remit them to SEBI in the prescribed manner.",
 ["Fees aren't collected yearly.",None,"They recur every three-year block.","Collection is three-yearly; it's the remittance to SEBI that's monthly."],
 "FPI Regs 2019, Second Schedule Part A(4)")
add("FEE/GRT/702","FEE",1,"Who sends the first fee to SEBI?",
 [["Applicant","Pays its fee with the application"],["DDP","Grants registration"],["Question","Who remits the fee to SEBI?"],["Timing","After grant"]],
 "Who remits it?",
 ["The FPI, directly","The DDP, on granting the certificate","NSDL","The global custodian"],1,
 "On granting the certificate, the DDP remits the fee it received from the applicant to SEBI.",
 ["The FPI pays the DDP, not SEBI directly.",None,"The depository doesn't remit FPI fees.","The global custodian has no remittance role."],
 "FPI Regs 2019, Reg 7(3)")
add("FEE/RLX/703","FEE",3,"Asking SEBI to relax a rule",
 [["FPI","Breached a procedural requirement due to a system outage"],["Plan","Apply to SEBI for relaxation"],["Question","What fee goes with the application?"],["Refundable","To be confirmed"]],
 "What's the fee?",
 ["None","US$1,000, non-refundable","US$2,500, refundable if rejected","US$250"],1,
 "SEBI may relax strict enforcement where non-compliance is beyond the entity's control or the requirement is procedural or technical. An FPI's application must carry a non-refundable fee of US$1,000.",
 ["Reg 43B prescribes a fee.",None,"The fee is US$1,000 and non-refundable.","US$250 is the Category II registration fee."],
 "FPI Regs 2019, Reg 43B")
add("FEE/DDP/704","FEE",2,"When the DDP approval fee is paid",
 [["Applicant","Proposed DDP"],["Paid","₹10,000 with the application"],["Question","When is the ₹5,00,000 approval fee due?"],["Status","Awaiting SEBI decision"]],
 "When is it due?",
 ["With the application","When SEBI grants approval, before activity starts","After the first year","It's waived for banks"],1,
 "A DDP pays the ₹10,000 application fee when applying, and the ₹5,00,000 approval fee when SEBI grants approval. Both must be paid before it starts activity.",
 ["Only the ₹10,000 goes with the application.",None,"It's due at grant, not after a year.","There's no waiver for banks."],
 "FPI Regs 2019, Second Schedule Part B")
add("FEE/REC/705","FEE",3,"Fees on the 2019 recategorisation",
 [["FPI","Category II under the 2014 Regulations"],["2019","Deemed recategorised to Category I"],["Question","Did it owe extra fees?"],["Later request","None"]],
 "Was any incremental fee payable?",
 ["Yes, the difference between the category fees","No incremental fee on deemed recategorisation","Yes, a flat US$500","Only on its next continuance"],1,
 "No incremental fee was payable on deemed recategorisation under the 2019 Regulations. An FPI that later asks to move from Category II to Category I pays the applicable fees.",
 ["The guidelines waived incremental fees for deemed recategorisation.",None,"There's no flat fee.","It didn't owe anything extra for the deemed move."],
 "Op. Guidelines Part A 1(v)")
